    "name": "gap_x_direction",
    "mechanism": "Digestion vs exhaustion after directional flow: an unusually long gap since the last trade (high z of trade_gap_ms) means the tape has gone quiet. WHAT the quiet follows determines its meaning: silence after one-sided buy aggression is either digestion (inventory absorbed, continuation) or exhaustion (move over, reversion). Direction-free gap levels cannot distinguish, which is why arrival/gap LEVELS died in iter-002; gating by the sign of the concurrent imbalance gives the market-state a direction. The IC sign then empirically resolves digestion vs exhaustion for 588000 at 30-300s horizons.",
    "info_set": "trade_gap_ms (wishlist), trade_imbalance_60s (library)",
    "inspiration": "iter-003 family brief seed 10; ACD/inter-trade-duration literature (Engle & Russell 1998; Lillo, Farmer & Mantegna 2003); iter-002 lesson that direction-free tape-state levels carry no IC.",
